    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44712" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">somnŭlentus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">somnŏl-</span></b> ), a,
		um, adj.
		somnus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>full of sleep</i>, i. e. <i>sleepy</i>, <i>drowsy</i>, <i>dozy</i>, <i>somnolent</i> (post-Aug.),
					<i><span class="en">App. M. 1 <i>fin.</i></span></i>; <i><span class="en">10</span></i>, p. 251, 37.—Hence,
				adv.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">somnŏlen-ter</span></b> , <i>sleepily</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Hier. in Psa. 118</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Sol. 20, 7</span></i>.</div>
